  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 15,
    "summary": "Eliphaz sets forth the disquietude of wicked men—They do not believe they will return out of darkness and be resurrected.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Then answered Eliphaz the Temanite, and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Should a wise man utter vain knowledge, and fill his belly with the east wind?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Should he reason with unprofitable talk? or with speeches wherewith he can do no good?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, thou castest off fear, and restrainest prayer before God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "For thy mouth uttereth thine iniquity, and thou choosest the tongue of the crafty.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Thine own mouth condemneth thee, and not I: yea, thine own lips testify against thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Art thou the first man that was born? or wast thou made before the hills?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 27
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Hast thou heard the secret of God? and dost thou restrain wisdom to thyself?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "What knowest thou, that we know not? what understandest thou, which is not in us?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 41
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "With us are both the grayheaded and very aged men, much elder than thy father.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 11
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Are the consolations of God small with thee? is there any secret thing with thee?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Why doth thine heart carry thee away? and what do thy eyes wink at,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "That thou turnest thy spirit against God, and lettest such words go out of thy mouth?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "What is man, that he should be clean? and he which is born of a woman, that he should be righteous?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "Ether 12:37; D&C 38:42."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ether 12:37; D&C 38:42.",
            "prettyString": "Ether 12:37; D&C 38:42",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "ether",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 12,
                    "end": 12,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 37,
                        "end": 37
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "doctrineandcovenants",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 38,
                    "end": 38,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 42,
                        "end": 42
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, he putteth no trust in his saints; yea, the heavens are not clean in his sight.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "IE God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "How much more abominable and filthy is man, which drinketh iniquity like water?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Filthiness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 38
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Filthiness.",
            "prettyString": "TG Filthiness",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Filthiness",
                "entryId": "tg-filthiness",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "I will shew thee, hear me; and that which I have seen I will declare;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 41
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Which wise men have told from their fathers, and have not hid it:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Unto whom alone the earth was given, and no stranger passed among them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "The wicked man travaileth with pain all his days, and the number of years is hidden to the oppressor.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "A dreadful sound is in his ears: in prosperity the destroyer shall come upon him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 19
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "He believeth not that he shall return out of darkness, and he is waited for of the sword.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "He wandereth abroad for bread, saying, Where is it? he knoweth that the day of darkness is ready at his hand.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:23",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "Trouble and anguish shall make him afraid; they shall prevail against him, as a king ready to the battle.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:24",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "For he stretcheth out his hand against God, and strengtheneth himself against the Almighty.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:25",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "He runneth upon him, even on his neck, upon the thick bosses of his bucklers:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 25
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:26",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Because he covereth his face with his fatness, and maketh collops of fat on his flanks.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "OR has grown fat on his loins."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 79
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:27",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "And he dwelleth in desolate cities, and in houses which no man inhabiteth, which are ready to become heaps.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 106,
            "text": "IE of ruins."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:28",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "He shall not be rich, neither shall his substance continue, neither shall he prolong the perfection thereof upon the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:29",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "He shall not depart out of darkness; the flame shall dry up his branches, and by the breath of his mouth shall he go away.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:30",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "Let not him that is deceived trust in vanity: for vanity shall be his recompence.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "TG Vanity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Vanity.",
            "prettyString": "TG Vanity",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Vanity",
                "entryId": "tg-vanity",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:31",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "It shall be accomplished before his time, and his branch shall not be green.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:32",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "He shall shake off his unripe grape as the vine, and shall cast off his flower as the olive.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 15:33",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 33
      },
      {
        "text": "For the congregation of hypocrites shall be desolate, and fire shall consume the tabernacles of bribery.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "TG Hypocrisy."
          },
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "TG Bribe."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 34,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Hypocrisy.",
            "prettyString": "TG Hypocrisy",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Hypocrisy",
                "entryId": "tg-hypocrisy",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "TG Bribe.",
            "prettyString": "TG Bribe",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
